WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.259
You walk into a room

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:03.168
and forget why you came.

00:00:03.518 --> 00:00:05.089
It happens to everyone.

00:00:05.439 --> 00:00:07.395
It is not your memory failing.

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:09.031
It is the doorway.

00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:11.483
Your brain chops life into events.

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.959
A doorway is an event boundary.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.319
It files away the last episode.

00:00:16.669 --> 00:00:18.262
So the goal gets buried.

00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:21.278
In experiments, people carried objects.

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:23.967
Same distance, with or without a door.

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:26.421
Those who crossed a door forgot more.

00:00:26.771 --> 00:00:29.586
Even returning to the first room did not help.

00:00:29.936 --> 00:00:31.966
The door itself triggers the reset.

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:34.026
But this chunking is useful.

00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:36.011
It keeps memories tidy.

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:38.390
To beat it, say your plan out loud.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.418
Or carry the thing you need.

00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:42.486
Or take one step back.

00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:44.779
Small trick. Big difference.

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:47.318
Next time, the doorway will not win.
